//! **Option B, step two — the activation lemmas over `ir_lzb_module`.**
//!
//! Ten frame-level facts and the three recursive segment lemmas that splice
//! them, all quantified over the caller's entire continuation.
//!
//! ## The one thing that differs from the hand model, and why
//!
//! Every peel of the step count here is an EXPLICIT `ir_steps_add` rewrite,
//! where `eval_ir_activation.rs` peels literal runs definitionally and
//! splices only the variable ones. That is not a style choice.
//! `ir_steps (Nat.succ f) M c` unfolds to an `IRConfig.rec` that must
//! case-analyse `c`, while `ir_steps W M _` at a VARIABLE cost `W` is a rigid
//! `Nat.rec`. A definitional peel asks the unifier to accept
//! `ir_steps (Nat.add W k) M c == ir_steps W M (ir_steps k M c)` across that
//! boundary, and it refuses with `Nat.rec vs IRConfig.rec`.
//!
//! The hand model never meets this: its recursive arms carry only VARIABLE
//! segments, which it already splices explicitly. This module has a LITERAL
//! segment — the deref model's seven steps — sitting inside a variable-cost
//! chain, and that is forced by the shape of the problem: an assumed callee
//! has a known, literal cost. So the peel that is free in the model is not
//! free here. Measured, same lemma both ways: definitional FAILS, explicit
//! PASSES.
//!
//! ## The four big terms are MINTED, not typed
//!
//! `SRC_IR_LZB_DEREF_ACTIVATION` and the three `*_SEG` constants below total
//! ~45k characters of `Eq.trans` / `ir_steps_add` / `Eq.subst` chain. They are
//! emitted by [`scripts/gen_lzb_activation.py`] from a list of execution
//! SEGMENTS, so the deref model's cost and return value live in one place
//! rather than in several hundred substrings.
//!
//! The generator's correctness argument is not a claim about its code: run
//! with the PRE-strengthening parameters — a five-step deref returning the
//! stored word — it reproduces, byte for byte, the four terms that were
//! hand-written and kernel-checked at `fc350b9c4` (2026-08-26). Those digests
//! are pinned in its `--self-test`, so a refactor that changes the emitted
//! shape fails there rather than in a spec build an hour later.
//!
//! ```text
//! python3 scripts/gen_lzb_activation.py --self-test   # the 08-26 terms
//! python3 scripts/gen_lzb_activation.py --check       # matches this file
//! ```
//!
//! `DerivedProved`, empty axiom closures.

